23:27:25 [bdba] - friendship development: Understanding how to make and maintain friendships. Skills: finding common interests, choosing appropriate peers, inviting someone to play, being a good host.
23:27:25 [bdba] - emotion understanding: Recognizing and discussing emotions in self and others. Skills: identifying basic emotions, linking emotions to causes, noticing facial, body, and context cues, expressing one's own feeling.
23:27:25 [bdba] - perspective taking theory of mind: Understanding that another person may think, know, feel, or want something different. Skills: identifying another person's belief, understanding different preferences, predicting how someone may react, explaining why someone acted a certain way.
23:27:25 [bdba] - cooperative play and group participation: Participating in games, group tasks, and shared activities. Skills: following game rules, taking turns, sharing materials, being flexible.
23:27:25 [bdba] - conflict resolution: Handling disagreement with peers in a safe and socially functional way. Skills: staying calm, using words to explain the problem, listening to the other person, suggesting a solution.
23:27:25 [bdba] - teasing bullying and rejection response: Responding to teasing, exclusion, or bullying safely. Skills: distinguishing playful joking from hurtful teasing, using a short response, walking away, seeking adult support.
23:27:25 [bdba] - social problem solving: Understanding a social problem and selecting an appropriate response. Skills: identifying the problem, thinking of possible solutions, predicting consequences, choosing a safe solution.
23:27:25 [bdba] - self advocacy and communication of needs: Expressing needs, boundaries, preferences, and requests for help. Skills: asking for a break, saying no appropriately, asking for clarification, explaining sensory needs.
